# Measured 2026-08-17: 13.9s on a clean pass, ~2s to reject (lint-staged fails first).
#
# That is within a second of pre-push, which is worth knowing: almost all of it is
# vitest's 6.7s and lint-staged's ~3s. Vitest is here because it was asked for, and the
# trade is deliberate — a commit that cannot pass its own tests is worth catching before
# it is written down. Drop `npm run test` from this file if the wait ever starts earning
# --no-verify; pre-push still runs it.
#
# What is here and what is not, deliberately:
#
#   lint-staged        eslint + prettier, staged files only — the architecture policies
#                      in eslint.config.js ride along with this
#   typecheck          2.3s, and a type error is not worth pushing
#   depcruise          cycles, orphans and transitive reach — the whole graph, not the diff
#   vitest             4.9s
#   check-test-shape   Given/When/Then, per docs/11
#
# The three sync gates and check:adherence run on push instead. Not because they are slow
# — together they are under 2s — but because sync:design, check:content and sync:cards all
# read the sibling design-system repo and exit 1 when it is absent. On push that is a fair
# demand; on every commit it would block a machine that has not cloned it yet.

npx lint-staged
npm run typecheck
npm run depcruise
npm run test
npm run check:test-shape
